{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, the customer needs to make a purchase and then connect to the website."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly triggers the init node and directly defines the start and first compound action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, they should search for an item."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the item search step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If they choose to \"Add item to cart\", they can proceed to checkout."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the XOR split point, the summarized choice action, the guard value matching the cart option, and the checkout action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if they select \"Continue Shopping\", they should continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps the alternative guard condition and the corresponding continue-shopping action arm."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once they proceed to checkout, they need to enter their address, shipping method, and payment information."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact description of the data entry step during checkout."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the same time, they should also authorize the credit card and check the inventory levels."
      ],
      "justification": "Timing phrase \"At the same time\" justifies the AND parallel split and converge, while the action captures both verification tasks."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "action:n10",
        "guard:b2->n10",
        "guard:b3->c2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the credit card is approved and there is inventory in stock, they can continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the positive validation path: completion check, approval/inventory check action, and guards routing toward the success convergence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n17",
        "guard:b3->n16",
        "action:n16",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the credit card is denied or there is no inventory in stock, the transaction will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the negative validation logic, denial/no-inventory guards, the termination actions, and the explicit transaction end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In either case, the order confirmation number should be displayed, followed by the final order being shown to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "\"In either case\" signals the post-decision convergence, immediately followed by the two display steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, the order should be confirmed and a confirmation notice should be emailed to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the order confirmation and email notification actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the order entry is complete, the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly defines the final completion checkpoint and the main process termination."
    }
  ],
